You could dive for Medusa and see if you can get a reflection source
there.  Of course, that means you must kill Medusa herself the hard
way.

Or just dive past Medusa for the Castle and use a wish.

You might try to look for other sources of wishes in the dungeon, but
the Castle wand is the only guaranteed one.  It's also possible to
find a random shield or amulet of reflection in a shop, or even just
lying around.

Silver dragons may drop scales.  Of course, Murphy's law says you'll
just keep getting more black dragons instead.

Or you could try to sneak up on the dragon, waiting for him behind a
corner so that he can't hit you from a distance (beware of bounces!),
and whack him with a rubber chicken as soon as he's in range.  If you
stand still and wait for him to come to you, you should be able to get
the first strike, especially if you're fast.  Telepathy, gloves and
the rubber chicken itself are required, of course.  Don't miss.

(Do dragons even use their breath weapons at melee range at all?  If
they don't, you should be safe as long as you can get next to him
without getting disintegrated and then stay next to him until he's
dead.  But I'm not sure if they do or not.)

A wand of sleep and/or a potion of paralysis might also work.

Anyway, if this was my game, I'd explore the Mines first (if you
haven't done that already) and then just dig past that level.  You
don't _have_ to come back up until you ascend.

Assuming this character is also a Valk, getting the Orb should make
skipping uncomfortable levels somewhat easier.

